sequenceDiagram
  participant glfw
  participant M as main.py<br/>MiniPaint
  participant T as tools.py<br/>Tool
  participant S as shapes.py<br/>Shape
  participant R as raster.py<br/>fill.py
  participant C as MiniPaint.canvas
  participant SC as MiniPaint.screen
  participant GL as OpenGL.GL

  Note over glfw,M: Você aperta o botão em cima do canvas
  glfw->>M: on_mouse_button(PRESS)
  opt Qualquer ferramenta menos o Mover
    M->>M: commit_selection()
    M->>S: selection.draw(canvas)
    M->>M: remember()
  end
  M->>T: press(canvas, x, y)
  Note over glfw,M: Você arrasta o mouse
  glfw->>M: on_cursor_move(x, y)
  M->>T: drag(canvas, x, y)
  alt Pincel, Lápis e Borracha pintam direto no canvas
    T->>R: draw_line(canvas, last, x, y)
    R->>R: bresenham_line(), stamp()
    R->>C: put_pixel(x, y, color)
  else Balde pinta no press
    T->>R: flood_fill(canvas, x, y, color)
    R->>C: get_pixel(), put_pixel()
  else Linha, Retângulo, Círculo, Polígono e Selecionar só guardam os pontos
    T->>T: start, end, vertices
  end

  loop A cada quadro, dentro de MiniPaint.run
    M->>SC: copy_from(canvas)
    M->>S: selection.draw(screen)
    M->>R: draw_dashed_rect(screen)
    M->>T: preview(screen)
    alt Linha, Retângulo e Círculo
      T->>T: make()
      T->>S: draw(screen)
      S->>R: draw_line(), draw_circle(), fill_polygon()
    else Polígono e Selecionar desenham a prévia direto
      T->>R: draw_line(), blend_rect(), draw_dashed_rect()
    end
    R->>SC: put_pixel(), put_span()
    M->>GL: glDrawPixels(screen.pixels)
  end

  Note over glfw,M: Você solta o botão
  glfw->>M: on_mouse_button(RELEASE)
  M->>T: release(canvas, x, y)
  T-->>M: Shape
  M->>M: select(shape)
  Note over M,S: A forma pronta vira <code>MiniPaint.selection</code>, solta por cima do canvas.<br/>O Polígono entrega a forma no press que fecha a figura ou no Enter.<br/>O <code>SelectTool.release</code> já copia os pixels e pinta o buraco no canvas.
